{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2193-04-14 20:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the surgical team. You're here because you were brought in after stabbing your urostomy with a screwdriver. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2193-04-14 20:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just... I felt very very sad. I didn’t know what else to do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2193-04-14 20:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m really sorry you’re feeling that way. Your safety is our priority. We’ve looked at your abdomen and there’s a wound near your urostomy. We’re concerned it may have gone deep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2193-04-14 20:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It hurts a lot in my lower right side. Is my stoma broken?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2193-04-14 20:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think the injury may have gone into the small intestine. That’s why it’s so painful. We’re going to take you to surgery tonight to fix it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2193-04-14 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Surgery? Again? I just had one a few months ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2193-04-14 20:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, an exploratory laparotomy. We need to open the abdomen to check for damage and repair any holes. We’ll also remove any debris and clean the area."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2193-04-14 20:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2193-04-14 20:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We believe so. The sooner we fix this, the better. You’re also getting a central line placed for fluids and meds. We’ve already done a chest X-ray to confirm it’s in the right spot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2193-04-14 20:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m scared."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2193-04-14 20:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely understandable. We’ll be with you every step. The anesthesiologist will talk to you before surgery. Rest now—we’ll take care of you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2193-04-15 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You made it through surgery. You had a laceration in your small intestine, which we repaired. We also had to do lysis of adhesions—scar tissue was pulling things together."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2193-04-15 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Did you fix my stoma too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2193-04-15 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The stoma itself wasn’t torn, but we placed a Foley catheter into it to keep it draining and reduce pressure while it heals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2193-04-15 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel nauseous. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2193-04-15 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, nausea is common after abdominal surgery. Your bowel is still waking up. We’re monitoring it. You’re not passing gas yet, which tells us it’s slow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2193-04-15 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How long will I be here?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2193-04-15 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "At least a few days. We need to make sure your gut starts working, you’re not leaking from the repair, and your pain is controlled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2193-04-15 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my sadness? Who’s helping with that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2193-04-15 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The psychiatry team is aware. They’ll come see you today. You’re not alone in this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2193-04-15 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in. Your vitals are stable, but your heart rate is a bit high. We’re watching it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2193-04-15 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel jittery. Is that from the pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2193-04-15 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’re avoiding certain ones because of your allergies. We’ll adjust as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2193-04-16 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—we did a loopogram yesterday, which is an X-ray test where we put contrast into your stoma. There’s no leak from your ileal conduit. That means the repair is holding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2193-04-16 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2193-04-16 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Very good. But the images also showed your small bowel is still distended. That’s expected after surgery—it’s called ileus. It’ll take time to recover."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2193-04-16 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I still can’t eat?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2193-04-16 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. You’re on IV fluids. We’ll start with small sips once your bowel starts moving. We’re waiting for you to pass gas."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2193-04-16 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I passed gas this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2193-04-16 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a great sign! Means your gut is waking up. We’ll start you on clear liquids today—water, broth, apple juice."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2193-04-16 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I have crackers?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2193-04-16 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We have to go slow. If you tolerate liquids, we’ll advance to soft foods tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2193-04-17 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well overnight. No nausea, and you kept down the liquids. We’re upgrading your diet to soft foods today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2193-04-17 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I sit up in a chair?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2193-04-17 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we encourage it. It helps your lungs and bowel. Physical therapy will come help you move safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2193-04-17 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The psych team came. They said I might need more help after I leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2193-04-17 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. They’re recommending outpatient mental health support. We also need to address housing—you mentioned you’re unhoused?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2193-04-17 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been staying in shelters. It’s hard with my wheelchair."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2193-04-17 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Our social worker is working on resources. There are programs for people with disabilities and medical needs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2193-04-18 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We removed the Foley from your stoma this morning. It’s draining normally."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2193-04-18 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Does that mean I’m healing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2193-04-18 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. The stoma looks healthy. We’ll keep monitoring your output and make sure there’s no blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2193-04-18 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m worried about my diabetes. My sugars have been high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2193-04-18 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re managing it with insulin. Stress and steroids can raise blood sugar. We’re adjusting your dose daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2193-04-18 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I usually take pills at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2193-04-18 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but in the hospital, insulin works faster and is safer for tight control. You’ll go back to oral meds when you’re home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2193-04-19 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news—you’re passing stool, and your diet is back to normal. We’re thinking you might be ready to go home in a day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2193-04-19 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? I thought I’d be here longer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2193-04-19 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve healed well. But we need to make sure your mental health and housing are set up before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2193-04-19 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The social worker said she found a shelter with wheelchair access and a clinic for my follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2193-04-19 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. And the psychiatry team is setting you up with counseling and medication management."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2193-04-20 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today we’ll do a final check. Your wound is clean, no signs of infection. You’re walking with the walker, eating well, and your stoma is functioning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2193-04-20 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2193-04-20 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send you home with a non-opioid pain reliever. Given your allergies and history, we’re avoiding narcotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2193-04-20 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to end up back here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2193-04-20 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We don’t either. That’s why the mental health support is so important. If you feel sad or unsafe, call your counselor or go to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2193-04-21 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All your labs look good. You’re medically ready for discharge. Social work is finalizing your shelter placement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2193-04-21 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I didn’t think I’d make it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2193-04-21 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re strong. Healing takes time—physically and emotionally. We’re here to support you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2193-04-22 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—your discharge is set for tomorrow morning. You’ll go with a walker and instructions for stoma care, diet, and meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2193-04-22 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up with urology and primary care?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2193-04-22 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, both in one week. We’ll send the records over. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2193-04-22 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2193-04-23 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Today’s the day. We’ll do a final check, give you your prescriptions, and get you discharged by noon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2193-04-23 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous but glad to leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2193-04-23 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s normal. Remember, you’re not alone. Call your team if anything changes—pain, fever, or emotional distress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2193-04-23 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I see my stoma before I go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2193-04-23 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. It looks healthy—pink, moist, and draining well. Keep the skin clean and use the barrier cream we showed you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2193-04-23 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll take care of it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2193-04-23 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re all set. Social work will escort you to the shelter. Take these prescriptions and follow-up slips."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2193-04-23 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. For everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2193-04-23 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care of yourself. We’re rooting for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2193-04-24 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick note to finalize your discharge. You’re officially discharged as of now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2193-04-24 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m already at the shelter. They’ve been nice."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2193-04-24 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. Keep up with your appointments. We’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2193-04-24 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I want to get better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2193-04-24 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you will. One day at a time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2193-04-24 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2193-04-24 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Stay safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2193-04-24 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2193-04-24 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s all we can ask."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2193-04-24 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll call if I need help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2193-04-24 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Please do. We’re here for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2193-04-24 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel like I have a chance now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2193-04-24 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You absolutely do. Take it one step at a time."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2193-04-14 20:20:00",
    "admission_end": "2193-04-24 12:23:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of paraplegia, neurogenic bladder, urostomy, type II diabetes, and polysubstance abuse was admitted after self-inflicting multiple stab wounds to her urostomy site with a screwdriver, reporting she felt 'very very sad.' She underwent an exploratory laparotomy and repair of a small intestinal laceration, along with lysis of adhesions. A Foley catheter was temporarily placed into the urostomy to aid healing. Postoperatively, she developed expected ileus, managed supportively. A loopogram confirmed no leak from the ileal conduit. She gradually advanced to a regular diet, regained bowel function, and was medically stable. Psychiatry and social work addressed her mood disorder, substance use, and housing instability. She was discharged to a wheelchair-accessible shelter with follow-up plans for mental health, primary care, and urology.",
    "problems": [
      "Other injury to small intestine, with open wound into cavity",
      "Paraplegia",
      "Body Mass Index 40.0-44.9, adult",
      "Late effect of spinal cord injury",
      "Morbid obesity",
      "Neurogenic bladder NOS",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Unspecified episodic mood disorder",
      "Lack of housing",
      "Cannabis abuse, unspecified",
      "Cocaine dependence, unspecified",
      "Suicide and self-inflicted injury by cutting and piercing instrument",
      "Accidents occurring in unspecified place",
      "Wheelchair dependence",
      "Nausea alone",
      "Tachycardia, unspecified",
      "Alcohol abuse, continuous",
      "Tobacco use disorder",
      "Below knee amputation status",
      "Unspecified hereditary and idiopathic peripheral neuropathy",
      "Attention to other artificial opening of urinary tract"
    ]
  }
}
